WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:06.020
Singer Lisa Marie Presley's cause of death
just revealed.

00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:10.740
The 54-year-old died from complications from
a prior weight loss surgery.

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:16.379
The report says it was, quote, a smoul bowel
obstruction caused by scar tissue that developed

00:00:16.379 --> 00:00:19.350
after a previous bariatric surgery years ago.

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:21.600
The manner of death is natural.

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:26.760
Joining us now is CNN chief medical correspondent
Dr. Sanjay Gupta.

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:28.189
Interested in what you have to say about this.

00:00:28.189 --> 00:00:33.630
Hearing of someone dying of obstruction in
the small intestine, but this was apparently

00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:37.760
a side effect of this kind of weight loss
surgery?

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:39.950
&gt;&gt; Right.

00:00:39.950 --> 00:00:44.989
Parts of this story make a lot of sense, and
parts are a little bit more unusual.

00:00:44.989 --> 00:00:49.670
What they are describing when they say that
there was a previous operation that led to

00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:53.590
this, anytime someone has an operation on
the abdomen, inside the belly, you can develop

00:00:53.590 --> 00:00:54.590
scar

00:00:54.590 --> 00:00:55.590
[8:40:32 AM]

00:00:55.590 --> 00:00:56.590
the belly, you can develop scar tissue.

00:00:56.590 --> 00:00:57.590
It's called adhesionens.

00:00:57.590 --> 00:01:04.890
Think of it like spiderwebs that develop and
they can constrict parts of the intestines.

00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:06.180
This takes place over time.

00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:08.780
Her previous operation was years ago.

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:13.740
Over time, it may actually compress parts
of the intestine to the point they about become

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.310
obstructed, strangelated.

00:01:15.310 --> 00:01:17.150
They are blocked, essentially.

00:01:17.150 --> 00:01:22.890
You are not getting food through and there
is not enough blood throw.

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:24.110
That happens.

00:01:24.110 --> 00:01:28.650
We know that that can happen and sometimes
people with off and on pain for some time.

00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:33.940
What is unusual, though, is it sounds like
maybe she had pain off and on, but the morning

00:01:33.940 --> 00:01:38.390
of she was complaining of some pain and then
was found unresponsive at her home, taken

00:01:38.390 --> 00:01:41.340
to the hospital where she subsequently died.

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:44.280
That was a very rapid time course.

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:45.280
That's a bit unusual.

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:49.450
Usually, if someone is in the hospital with
this sort of thing, they can even go back

00:01:49.450 --> 00:01:54.870
in and operate, do something to relieve that
blockage, but she had progressed so far, sounds

00:01:54.870 --> 00:01:55.870
[8:41:32 AM]

00:01:55.870 --> 00:01:58.070
had progressed so far, sounds like, by the
time she got to the hospital that she passed

00:01:58.070 --> 00:01:59.070
away.

00:01:59.070 --> 00:02:05.000
So it can happen, but these blockages as with
result of scar tissue, but the idea that they

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:08.830
lead to death, especially that quickly, was
more unusual.

00:02:08.830 --> 00:02:12.620
It's really sad, the situation that unfolded
there.

00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:16.330
&gt;&gt; The report also listed therapeutic and
not dangerous levels of oxycontin.

00:02:16.330 --> 00:02:21.459
Can medications like that play a role in something
like this?

00:02:21.459 --> 00:02:27.140
&gt;&gt; It's interesting because I think when someone
dies quickly, you think did a medication lead

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:30.690
to that, did it interfere with their act to
breathe on their own.

00:02:30.690 --> 00:02:33.400
That's not the case here, sounds like from
the report.

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:35.810
Two ways it might contribute though.

00:02:35.810 --> 00:02:40.349
One is that what I just described earlier
could be painful.

00:02:40.349 --> 00:02:44.239
And opioids, other medications can mask that
pain.

00:02:44.239 --> 00:02:46.590
Someone may go to the hospital a little bit
later as a result.

00:02:46.590 --> 00:02:51.970
The second thing is, opioids can also further
slow down your intestines.

00:02:51.970 --> 00:02:55.080
So a blockage that was already unfolding could
have been made

